[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474924251","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99188#issuecomment-2474924251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99188","id":2474924251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ThFjb","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T22:08:31Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T22:08:31Z","body":"I changed the behavior of the options visibility and disabled state a bit to hide/disable controls that are not editing anything right now:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c053869f-cd75-4b3d-b437-c617f5ee6054\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474924251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475129443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99188#issuecomment-2475129443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99188","id":2475129443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Th3pj","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T00:56:24Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T16:32:05Z","body":"Hi, you haven't handled the backwards compatibility properly it looks like. \r\n\r\nYou may not remove/rename public functions (only major versions like 5.0 may break API like this). Instead, deprecate the old one and refer to the new one in the deprecation message. \r\n\r\nAdding a new parameter in the middle is also an issue. Either needs to be a new method, or the new parameter must be at the end of the list and be optional. In that case follow these instructions https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/development/handling_compatibility_breakages.html\r\n\r\nAlso when adding to the `.expected` file, you should provide an explanation of why this isn't a breaking API change (e.g. \"New default parameter at end of list. Compatibility method registered.\")\r\n\r\nHope this helps!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475129443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475651799","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99188#issuecomment-2475651799","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99188","id":2475651799,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tj3LX","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T07:56:08Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T07:56:08Z","body":"@RedMser Helped a lot, thank you!\r\n\r\nI hope my compat handling of the deprecated `get_transition_fade_beats` method is fine as it is now.\r\n\r\n- It will always return the fade length even if the unit is not \"beats\" anymore\r\n- This should be fine because when upgrading from an earlier version of Godot, everything has a unit of \"beats\" because nothing else existed before\r\n- When using the deprecated `get_transition_fade_beats` on a transition that has been set to use another unit than \"beats\" I print a warning that the return value is likely not what is expected from the (deprecated) function name and what methods to use instead.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475651799/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475688954","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99188#issuecomment-2475688954","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99188","id":2475688954,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TkAP6","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T08:17:09Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T08:17:09Z","body":"Some thoughts about renaming the method `add_transition` to `add_transition_with_unit`:\r\n\r\n- If we would want to keep the old name, the new parameter would need to go to the end of the parameter list. That would mean users need to provide values for `use_filler_clip` and `filler_clip` only to provide the unit. Also the unit would not be next to the value anymore:\r\n  ```gdscript\r\n  add_transition(0, 2, 0.0, 0.0, FADE_CROSS, 2.5, false, -1, UNIT_SECONDS)\r\n  ```\r\n  vs\r\n  ```gdscript\r\n  add_transition_with_unit(0, 2, 0.0, 0.0, FADE_CROSS, 2.5, UNIT_SECONDS)\r\n  ```\r\n- The method could be renamed back to `add_transition` in the next major release because in the end the additional `_with_unit` suffix has no other reason than preserving compatibility.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475688954/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476844885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99188#issuecomment-2476844885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99188","id":2476844885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ToadV","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T16:18:12Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T16:32:13Z","body":"Looks a lot better! It makes sense to me that the old API \"works like before\", as long as you're only using beats.\r\n\r\n> I hope my compat handling of the deprecated `get_transition_fade_beats` method is fine as it is now.\r\n\r\nAlmost... The `.compat.inc` file is only needed if you're *changing* an existing method in such a way that it breaks compat (e.g. adding a new parameter, even if it is a default parameter)[^1]. Since you renamed it from _beats to _length, this is still a breaking change, as shown in the [checks](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/11833048306/job/32971007931?pr=99188):\r\n\r\n```\r\nError: Validate extension JSON: API was removed: classes/AudioStreamInteractive/methods/get_transition_fade_beats\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you go into GDScript you'd also get an error trying to use the _beats method, since it is not bound anymore. The \"compat\" bindings are only there to basically say \"if you make a GDExtension and it is targetting an old API, use this compat method so that the API looks the same as it did back when you compiled it\".\r\n\r\nFor your case, you can simply\r\n\r\n- remove the `.compat.inc` file\r\n- wrap the _beats method code (cpp and h) in a DISABLE_DEPRECATED ifdef\r\n- bind the method (also DISABLE_DEPRECATED) like a normal method\r\n- re-add it to the docs with the deprecated annotation\r\n- EDIT: ideally the extension API validator shouldn't fail if you only add new methods and mark old ones as deprecated, so the changes to the diff file should be removed too\r\n\r\n[^1]: My understanding: Basically the engine computes a hash for each binded member of each class. So if you change anything that modifies \"how the API looks like\" to the engine, you'll get an error in the extension API validator. Only adding completely new members or classes is allowed without further intervention.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476844885/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476881642","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99188#issuecomment-2476881642","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99188","id":2476881642,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tojbq","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T16:31:50Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T16:31:50Z","body":"Compat stuff looks good to me now, if the CI also does not complain 😉 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476881642/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476886987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99188#issuecomment-2476886987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99188","id":2476886987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TokvL","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T16:33:39Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T16:33:39Z","body":"@RedMser thanks a lot for the detailed explanation! :raised_hands:  CI should be fine after the latest push :smile: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476886987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/25183